      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-10-01_WidnesExaminer_art0095" n="art0095">
        <head>MAIN AT CROFT.</head>
        <p>MAIN AT CROFT.</p>
        <p>On Saturday the members of the Croft Bowling Club held their closing malt on the green at the Horseshoe Inn. Some excellent contests took place with the following result :-1, S. Taylor; 2, A. Houghton ; Jas. Shaw: 4, H. Shaw ; 5, H. Hankinson. After tea Mr. J. Shaw occupied the chair, and presented the prizes to the successful competitors. The balance sheet, which was read by the Secretary, showed the club to be in a healthy condition. The officers for the coming year were also elected as follows :—President, Mr. J. Shaw; vice-president, Mr. T. Oakes; treasurer, Mr. J. Maines ; and Messrs. H. Hankmson and W. Hatton as joint secre- taries. A smoking concert was afterwards held.</p>
        <p>COVE N TRY</p>
